# What the build context must not carry.
#
# Two kinds of thing are excluded, and only the second is about size. The
# runtime artifacts are excluded because they are *per-machine*: a corpus and
# the relevance floor measured for it describe one store under one embedding
# model, a run snapshot describes one afternoon, and baking either into an
# image would ship one machine's measurements to every other. They arrive
# through the bind mount instead, which is where they belong.

# The host's virtualenv: 1.3 GB, built for the host's interpreter, and the
# image builds its own at /opt/venv.
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Caches. .mypy_cache alone is ~174 MB of the context.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Per-machine runtime state (see above), and what an older console left under
# knowledge/ before the corpus moved into PostgreSQL.
knowledge/chroma/
knowledge/knowledge_graph.json
knowledge/floor_calibration.json
knowledge.lock
runs/
uploads/
research/web/
projects/
reports/diagnostics/
experimental/

# Credentials, never the image's. .env reaches the container through the bind
# mount, which keeps it on the host where it can be edited and is not baked
# into a layer anyone can pull apart.
.env

# Editor and VCS noise the build has no use for.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
*.log

# The Docker-only install's own settings and SearxNG config (docker/install.sh):
# this machine's, never the image's.
docker/.env
docker/searxng/
